# Renter communications privacy

Automatic emails and texts to renters require **per-renter consent** (`people.auto_communications_enabled`, default off).

Tenant SMS uses Sent (`sentNotify.js`) dual-channel with ACS email. Same consent and one-off rules apply to both channels.

## Rules for agents

- Never enable automatic communications without staff recording consent on the person record.
- Never add silent, scheduled, or bulk tenant email/SMS paths that bypass consent.
- One-off tenant messages are allowed only via **explicit staff actions** (dedicated button or a default-off `notify` checkbox the office manager opts into).
- Creating invoices must not imply email/SMS. Catch-up and period create default to `notify: false`.
- `RENT_COMMUNICATIONS_ENABLED` / `PREVIEW` gate the **daily auto scheduler** (plus preview routing). They do not replace per-renter consent. One-off sends use ACS/Sent directly; preview still redirects email to `CONTACT_NOTIFY_EMAIL` and SMS to `ALERT_PHONE`.
- Staff/ops digests and alert SMS (office pager via Sent + `ALERT_PHONE`) are not renter communications and are out of scope for this rule.
- Dual-send: attempt email when on file and SMS when phone + Sent are configured; log when either channel succeeds.
